{"kind":"report","text":"Disposition of the checker's P3 7e114bac on scope contract revision 23, witness 18.53 cases 9 and 22. The finding is right: the stand-in job type starts in the state queued and requires its two fixed references, ticket and owner, with no defaults, so the stand-in rule open-stopped cannot open a job directly in the state gone with most.effects 2; by the contract's rule on a rule's output (EJ10 and section 6.1) an item is opened in its initial state with every required fixed slot set, and an opening in another state is a fault. Corrected representation, to be written into the contract's next revision as owner of the witness: open-stopped states most: { opens: 1, effects: 4 } and yields four effects in this order: open one job (it takes the initial state queued); set its fixed reference ticket from the message's field; set its fixed reference owner from the sender; set its state to gone. No other form is used and no bound is waived; cases 9 and 22 keep their answers, since the binding and the index read the job as the folded state before the entry holds it. The same holds for the adopted case it stands for, which the authority note owns: its row for a withdraw before its reserve has the rule open-withdrawn open a publication as not-reserved. The authority note's next revision will restate that row as: open the publication in its initial state queued with its required fixed slots (the operation reference that is its index key, and the others its item type requires), then set the state not-reserved, with the rule's most restated to the count of those effects, and with the publication's holds and the reservation that the opening entry needs stated for an item that is final in the entry that opens it (already an open ask of that note to the contract). Owners: the builder as author of both notes; contract revision 24 for the witness, authority revision 29 for the row. This is a prose correction of an illustration and of one adopted row's representation; it claims nothing about source or capacity."}